  "title": "US President Donald Trump and Canada Continue Trade Name Debate Over Lake Ontario",
  "summary": "Meanwhile, the U.S. president announced new signs at the border, and Canada is responding with a different name, while the two countries continue their verbal spat over trade tensions, including escalating tariffs.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. president announced new signs at the border, with the country erecting a sign reading 'Lake Ontario. Now and Always' and replacing it with 'Lake America' in a video.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Canadian government and public are preparing for the increase in tariffs, while the U.S. president plans to finalize a deal to avoid economic strain.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The two countries are involved in a trade dispute, with the U.S. government imposing tariffs on Canadian steel.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
